builder_directive_case fires on each wrong-cased builder directive in a
data source (`:dsn`, `:TableName`, `:NullAsBlank`, `:invariantDateColumns`):
the builder matches directives case-sensitively and silently ignores these.
The message names the uppercase form and the range covers the token.
-- input.ds --
:dsn := DATABASE;
:TableName := toolList;
:NullAsBlank := true;
:invariantDateColumns := issued_on;
:PARAMETERS sBin := "A1";

SELECT tool_id, issued_on FROM tool_issue WHERE bin_code = @sBin
-- format --
:dsn := DATABASE;
:TableName := toolList;
:NullAsBlank := true;
:invariantDateColumns := issued_on;
:PARAMETERS sBin := "A1";

SELECT tool_id, issued_on FROM tool_issue WHERE bin_code = @sBin
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:5 error builder_directive_case: Builder directives must be uppercase: use ':DSN'
2:1-2:11 error builder_directive_case: Builder directives must be uppercase: use ':TABLENAME'
3:1-3:13 error builder_directive_case: Builder directives must be uppercase: use ':NULLASBLANK'
4:1-4:22 error builder_directive_case: Builder directives must be uppercase: use ':INVARIANTDATECOLUMNS'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:5 error builder_directive_case: Builder directives must be uppercase: use ':DSN'
2:1-2:11 error builder_directive_case: Builder directives must be uppercase: use ':TABLENAME'
3:1-3:13 error builder_directive_case: Builder directives must be uppercase: use ':NULLASBLANK'
4:1-4:22 error builder_directive_case: Builder directives must be uppercase: use ':INVARIANTDATECOLUMNS'
